  "title": "Alphawaves dataset",
  "description": "Resting-state EEG recordings from 19 healthy participants who alternated between eyes-closed and eyes-open conditions in 10-second trials. Data were acquired with a 16-channel g.tec g.USBamp system at 512 Hz to study posterior alpha-band (8-12 Hz) modulation. The dataset is distributed in BIDS format via MOABB and originates from the GIPSA-lab Alpha Waves dataset.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded from 16 wet electrodes (standard 10-10 positions) with a g.tec g.USBamp amplifier at 512 Hz, referenced to the right earlobe, using OpenViBE software with no online digital filter. Subjects alternated between eyes-closed and eyes-open conditions in 10-second trials, with one session per subject.",
